ches for  more than 150 miles along florida's east  coast and the reason they're starving is  because their food is disappearing  manatees are vegetarians and often  called sea cows because they eat a lot  of sea grass more than 100 pounds a day  but for about a decade now the sea grass  has been disappearing that's because of  human-caused water pollution from  florida's development boom mainly sewage  from septic systems and fertilizer  runoff from nearby farms that helped  fuel a recent series of algae super  blooms in florida they darken the water  and block out the sun killing the sea  grass the manatees are left struggling  to find food we think we're right at the  tipping point dennis hannisack is a  researcher at the harbor branch  oceanographic institute where they're  experimenting with growing seagrass in  these large tanks and then transplanting  it into the lagoon to try to restore  some of the lost sea grass beds how much  sea grass has been lost 60 to 80 percent  if you look maybe at the whole lagoon by  some estimates repairing the massive  lagoon will require 5 billion dollars  and much tougher pollution rules so for  now desperate animal welfare  organizations have even resorted to hand  feeding manatees romaine lettuce  good job guys more than 130 manatees  have been rescued this year and slowly  nursed back to health this manatee  anastasia had lost much of her body  weight but in october she was strong  enough to be released  burcham says it's humans that caused  this problem and we need to fix it it's  not going to be a quick fix i strongly  believe if we all work together and we  all do our part we can still make a  difference  for cbs morning's ben tracy vero beach  florida  i love this story i love what ben's able  to do with these stories that he tells  he sets it up so beautifully you see  these beautiful pictures of manatees you  see the handlers who know them by name  yes and then he explains by the way  we're killing them because of pollution  in the water but then goes on to say we  still can do something about it save  them we're saying it's awesome yeah  humans cause this problem and now humans  fix it they can fix it right space was  produced by superb energy this is really  great i really enjoyed it really great

